# Docker build context exclusions (ADR-0016 — dotenvx migration; secret
# model). infra/docker/*.Dockerfile's `build` stage runs `COPY . .` against
# the repo root context (infra/docker/docker-compose.yml's `context: ../..`)
# — anything not excluded here is sent to the Docker daemon and can land in
# an intermediate layer, so real/example secrets, git history, and
# host-machine build output never belong in this list's absence.

# Host-machine, non-reproducible build output — the image installs its own
# dependencies and rebuilds from source (see the Dockerfiles' `deps`/`build`
# stages); copying the host's own node_modules would be wasted, oversized,
# and potentially platform-mismatched (native addons built for the host OS).
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
build/
.next/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
packages/infrastructure/src/generated/

# Never send real, example, or encrypted secret material into the build
# context. The build stage's own placeholder DATABASE_URL is set via
# Dockerfile `ENV`, never a .env file; real runtime secrets are injected by
# the deployment platform's secret store at container start, never baked
# into an image layer (see docs/adr/0016-dotenvx-environment-workflow.md).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.keys
.env.*.keys

.git/
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Dev-only local media storage stand-in; never shipped in an image.
.var/

# Pi-only E2E suite, QA proofing renders, and one-off editing tools —
# deliberately outside the pnpm workspace and irrelevant to any image build.
e2e/
qa/
tools/
docs/
